SHOULD (none blocks signing; each is a row that will otherwise cost a phase-2 round)
a. 5(j) vs the file-wide FIFO rule (327-330, 485-492). If the test opens the FIFO O_RDWR "before anything can block on it", a blocking open() finds a writer and returns at once
   (probed: pre-held O_RDWR opens in 0 ms; no writer parks until the 1.5 s timer), so 5(j) answers `not-regular` even without O_NONBLOCK and the row cannot catch the omission.
   Say 5(j) is exempt: the FIFO is created inside `afterLstat`, opened O_RDWR by the test only in the `finally`, after the opener has answered.
b. 15 (652-653): `verdict --from <file>` stamps `# tree: dirty:<hash>` if the transcript lives in the repo working tree outside studio/ (probed: header went dirty, then verify#2 stayed
   `verifying` because the predicate fail-closes on `dirty:`). Put the transcript under os.tmpdir() outside the repo, or under studio/.
c. 11(h) (587-591) never says its review logs carry the full verdict header; the predicate fail-closes without `opus:`, so an "older tree" log written as a bare `# tree:` line
   stays `verifying` instead of `review`. Say "full header" for all of 11 as 13 does.
d. nit: apps/server tsconfig includes test/, so a literal `await import("../src/branchRecords.js")` in branch-records.test.ts is TS2307 on the phase-1 commit (the brief already
   casts `branchGitTimeoutMs` for the same reason); use a computed specifier or a cast.
